WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.338
Good afternoon, Canada.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.878
I must tell you,

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.288
I took four years

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.557
of French in school.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:27.494
The first time I attempted

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:30.930
to make a speech in French

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.133
I was laughed at

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.369
So that's as good as I can get.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.104
No, no, I'm serious.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.573
And thank you very, very much.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.475
Speaker of the House of Commons.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.144
Speaker of the Senate.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.745
Member of the Parliament.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.680
Thank you for the very kind. Welcome.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.416
My wife and I.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.550
Prime Minister Trudeau,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.185
you were my first meeting

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.720
with a foreign leader

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.955
just one month after my presidency.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.325
During the hardest days of COVID 19.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.195
We had to make our visit virtual.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.696
But since then

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.231
we've been all over the world

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:05.999
talking and

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.301
taking on some of the toughest issues

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.302
our nations have faced

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.937
in a very long time.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.073
Well, thank you for your partnership.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.841
And for your personal friendship.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.444
I thank you very much for doing

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.048
so.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.616
Are grateful for the

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.885
hospitality you and Sophie have shown us.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.654
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.122
honored to have the opportunity

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.657
to uphold a tradition

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.224
carried out

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.792
by so many of my predecessors

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.760
in addressing

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.727
the hallowed halls

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.362
of the Canadian democracy.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.932
Although this is a different hall

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.968
that you've done a hell of a job.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.236
This is really beautiful.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.271
It is really very beautiful.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.807
This is, of course, in the space

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.043
The closeness of our relationship.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.612
Americans and Canadians are two people,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.147
two countries,

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.783
in my view, sharing one heart.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.252
It's for personal connection.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.888
No two nations on Earth are bound

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.589
by such close

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.557
ties friendship, family,

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.726
commerce and culture.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.229
Our labor unions cross borders.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.297
So do our sports leagues.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.701
Baseball, basketball, hockey

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.570
facilities, hockey,

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:21.107
I have to say that except the Leafs

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.646
for you on

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.185
I'm sure you are

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:38.391
I'll tell you alive

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.562
They beat the fliers back in January.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.030
That's why.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.798
And if I didn't see that

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.866
I married a Philly girl,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.434
if I didn't say that, I'd be sleeping

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:48.768
alone.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:51.771
Fellas, I like it, but not that much.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.777
It can be easy

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.512
to take a partnership between Canada

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.681
and the United States as a given

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.950
and but when you stop

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.219
and think about it, it's really a wonder.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.889
5552 mile long border.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.693
More than 8800 kilometers defined by

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.662
peaceful commerce,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.130
trading relationships that measured

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.567
more than $2.5 billion a day.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.335
Every day,

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.670
hundreds of thousands of people

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.637
cross the borders,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.574
going to north and south to work

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:28.741
or just to visit, knowing

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.709
they'll find a warm

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.244
welcome on the other side of the border.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.213
Americans

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.481
love Canadians, and that's not hyperbole.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.417
It's a data driven fact.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:38.351
Earlier this week,

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.087
the Gallup poll did a new poll showing

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.555
American opinions

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.357
on different countries in the world.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.392
This is a fact.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.595
Canada ranked at the very top.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.598
88% favorable rating

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:55.001
among Americans

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.874
Up from 87 the year before.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.445
I take credit for that one point

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:08.314
I suspect

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.283
every politician in this

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.085
this room would die

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.052
would do a hell of a lot

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.421
to get those kind of numbers

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.157
But there's a reason for it.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.892
The same fundamental aspiration

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:20.827
reverberate across

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.262
both our nations

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.697
from the Atlantic to the Pacific.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.432
To live in freedom,

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.433
not just freedom, to live in

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.802
freedom with dignity, with dignity,

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.005
to relentlessly pursue

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.941
the possibilities of tomorrow.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.043
To leave, leave our children

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:37.777
and our grandchildren

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.279
a future that's better

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.680
because of our efforts.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.682
The people in this room and similar

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.050
room in the United States.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.286
President Kennedy said.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.421
And when he spoke here in 1961

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.223
and I quote,

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:50.556
he said,

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:53.092
Ours is the unity of equal

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.961
and independent nations

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.363
quote tenants of the same continent.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.699
Heirs of the same legacy

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.734
and fully sovereign associates

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.037
in the same historic endeavor.

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:06.639
To preserve freedom for ourselves

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.675
and for all who wish it.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.377
For all who wish it

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.713
through more than a century.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.515
Of that historic endeavor, Canada,

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.916
the United States have had

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.886
each other's backs in war and in peace.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.589
We have been the stronghold of liberty,

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.792
safeguard

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.160
for the fundamental freedoms

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.162
that give us our lives.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:32.098
Literally, you give our lives meaning.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.499
We have gladly stepped

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.734
into the responsibilities

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.302
of global leadership

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:37.503
because we understand

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.105
all that is at risk

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:41.441
for Canadians and Americans alike.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:42.809
When freedom is under attack

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:45.311
anywhere in the world today.

00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:48.481
Our destinies are intertwined,

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.283
and they're inseparable,

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:50.883
not because

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:53.252
of the inevitability of geography.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.121
But because it's a choice,

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.523
a choice we've made again and again.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:58.891
The United

00:05:58.891 --> 00:05:59.759
States chooses to

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.295
link our future with Canada

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:04.530
because we know it will find

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.466
no better partner.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.501
I mean it to the bottom of my heart.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:11.070
No more reliable ally,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.039
no more steady friend.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.974
And today I say to you,

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:16.909
to all the people of Canada,

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.344
that you will always,

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.645
always be able to count

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.180
on the United States of America

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.382
a guarantee

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:38.998
together

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.573
Together we build a partnership that is

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.276
an incredible advantage.

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.145
To both our nations.

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:54.781
That doesn't mean we never disagree,

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.015
as any two countries

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:57.984
will do from time to time.

00:06:57.984 --> 00:06:59.719
But when we disagree,

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.088
we solve our differences in friendship

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.623
and in good will,

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:04.824
because we both understand

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:07.059
our interests are fundamentally aligned

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:09.962
as we stand at this inflection point.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.063
In history

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.231
that a professor

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:14.300
who once explained in a fashion point

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.635
as you're going down the highway

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:17.336
60 miles an hour

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.672
and you rapidly turn one direction

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.007
