everyone knows someone

00:22:42.627 --> 00:22:44.596
who has been affected by this.

00:22:44.596 --> 00:22:47.032
Lost a child or lost a friend.

00:22:47.032 --> 00:22:48.233
Canada and the United States

00:22:48.233 --> 00:22:49.534
are working closely

00:22:49.534 --> 00:22:50.669
with our partner in Mexico

00:22:50.669 --> 00:22:53.004
to attack this problem at every stage.

00:22:53.605 --> 00:22:54.439
From the precursor

00:22:54.439 --> 00:22:56.842
chemicals shipped from overseas

00:22:56.842 --> 00:22:58.543
to the powders to the pills,

00:22:58.543 --> 00:23:00.011
to the traffickers

00:23:00.011 --> 00:23:02.647
moving into all of our countries

00:23:02.647 --> 00:23:05.450
and we all know synthetic opioid

00:23:06.051 --> 00:23:08.420
epidemic has its roots around the globe,

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.255
not just here.

00:23:10.255 --> 00:23:11.923
So today we're announcing a commitment

00:23:11.923 --> 00:23:14.393
to build a new global coalition

00:23:14.393 --> 00:23:15.560
of like minded countries

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:16.895
led by Canada and the United States

00:23:16.895 --> 00:23:18.630
to tackle this crisis.

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:19.865
This is about public health

00:23:22.334 --> 00:23:22.768
It's about

00:23:22.768 --> 00:23:24.069
public health

00:23:36.515 --> 00:23:37.716
It's about public health,

00:23:37.716 --> 00:23:39.518
our economic futures,

00:23:39.518 --> 00:23:41.887
our national security

00:23:41.887 --> 00:23:43.355
We're also working together to address

00:23:43.355 --> 00:23:44.923
the record levels of migration

00:23:44.923 --> 00:23:46.224
in the hemisphere.

00:23:46.224 --> 00:23:47.626
Los Angeles Declaration

00:23:47.626 --> 00:23:49.428
on Migration and Protection,

00:23:49.428 --> 00:23:50.262
which the United States

00:23:50.262 --> 00:23:51.630
and Canada signed last June,

00:23:51.630 --> 00:23:53.698
along with 19 other nations,

00:23:53.698 --> 00:23:55.700
represents an integrated new approach

00:23:56.034 --> 00:23:57.569
to the migration challenge,

00:23:57.569 --> 00:23:59.004
which is a real

00:23:59.004 --> 00:24:01.373
one that unites humane policies,

00:24:01.373 --> 00:24:03.008
the most secure borders

00:24:03.008 --> 00:24:05.610
and support people in the United States.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:06.344
We're expanding

00:24:06.344 --> 00:24:08.246
legal pathways for migration

00:24:08.246 --> 00:24:10.081
to seek safety and humanitarian

00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:12.083
and humanitarian basis,

00:24:12.083 --> 00:24:13.084
while discouraging

00:24:13.084 --> 00:24:14.553
unlawful migration

00:24:14.553 --> 00:24:15.987
that feeds exploitation

00:24:15.987 --> 00:24:17.456
and human trafficking.

00:24:17.456 --> 00:24:20.358
So today, I applaud China for stepping up

00:24:20.392 --> 00:24:20.792
excuse me.

00:24:20.792 --> 00:24:23.562
I applaud Canada

00:24:24.362 --> 00:24:27.566
I can tell what I'm thinking

00:24:27.966 --> 00:24:28.633
about China.

00:24:28.633 --> 00:24:30.235
I won't get into that yet.

00:24:30.235 --> 00:24:30.635
I applaud

00:24:30.635 --> 00:24:32.671
Canada stepping up with similar programs,

00:24:32.671 --> 00:24:34.473
opening new legal pathways

00:24:34.473 --> 00:24:36.842
for 1500 migrants to come to Canada

00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:38.343
from countries in the Western Hemisphere.

00:24:38.343 --> 00:24:39.978
At the same time,

00:24:39.978 --> 00:24:40.645
the United States

00:24:40.645 --> 00:24:41.112
and Canada

00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:42.380
will work together to discourage

00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:43.949
unlawful border crossings

00:24:43.949 --> 00:24:45.150
and fully implement

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:46.151
and the updated

00:24:46.151 --> 00:24:48.119
Safe Third Country Agreement

00:25:02.167 --> 00:25:04.202
Finally, as we advance

00:25:04.202 --> 00:25:06.571
our shared prosperity and security,

00:25:06.571 --> 00:25:07.472
we must never lose

00:25:07.472 --> 00:25:09.608
sight of our shared values

00:25:09.608 --> 00:25:11.776
because our values literally the linchpin

00:25:12.477 --> 00:25:15.146
holding everything else together.

00:25:15.146 --> 00:25:17.015
Welcome refugees and seeking

00:25:17.015 --> 00:25:18.917
asylum seekers

00:25:18.917 --> 00:25:20.352
is a part of who Canadians

00:25:20.352 --> 00:25:22.220
and Americans are In fact,

00:25:22.220 --> 00:25:23.522
the United States recently

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:24.689
launched a new private

00:25:24.689 --> 00:25:26.691
sponsorship program for refugees.

00:25:27.125 --> 00:25:29.461
We call it Welcome Corps,

00:25:29.461 --> 00:25:30.061
which draws

00:25:30.061 --> 00:25:32.464
Canadian Canadians decades of leadership

00:25:32.464 --> 00:25:34.432
in refugee resettlement,

00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:35.300
where both countries

00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:36.835
build upon the nation to nation

00:25:36.835 --> 00:25:37.969
relationship

00:25:37.969 --> 00:25:40.305
with Native Americans and First Nations.

00:25:40.939 --> 00:25:41.172
We've

00:25:41.172 --> 00:25:42.207
both been influenced

00:25:42.207 --> 00:25:42.774
and strengthened

00:25:42.774 --> 00:25:43.742
by the contributions

00:25:43.742 --> 00:25:45.810
of a generation of immigrants.

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:47.846
We believe to our core

00:25:47.846 --> 00:25:49.147
that every single person

00:25:49.147 --> 00:25:51.616
deserves to live in dignity safety

00:25:52.150 --> 00:25:52.817
and rise

00:25:52.817 --> 00:25:54.920
as high as their dreams can carry them.

00:25:55.987 --> 00:25:58.223
We strive to defend human rights,

00:25:58.223 --> 00:26:00.792
to advance equality and gender equality

00:26:01.059 --> 00:26:02.727
to pursue justice

00:26:02.727 --> 00:26:04.195
and uphold the rule of law.

00:26:05.163 --> 00:26:06.898
I want to note the outstanding work

00:26:06.898 --> 00:26:08.733
Canada has done to build a coalition

00:26:08.733 --> 00:26:11.102
of nearly 70 countries

00:26:11.102 --> 00:26:12.437
endorsing the Declaration

00:26:12.437 --> 00:26:14.339
Against Arbitrary Detention

00:26:14.339 --> 00:26:17.342
and State-to-state Relations

00:26:22.380 --> 00:26:24.983
It's not only a statement of values.

00:26:24.983 --> 00:26:26.284
Our citizens are citizens,

00:26:26.284 --> 00:26:27.586
not bargaining chips.

00:26:27.586 --> 00:26:29.354
They're not diplomatic leverage.

00:26:29.354 --> 00:26:30.855
They're human beings

00:26:30.855 --> 00:26:32.090
with lives and families

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:33.692
that must be respected.

00:26:33.692 --> 00:26:36.027
And I'm very glad to see the two Michaels

00:26:36.928 --> 00:26:39.998
to Mike of Michael Schiavo and microphone

00:26:41.433 --> 00:26:45.036
for safely back to their families

00:26:45.804 --> 00:26:48.840
after more than 1000 days

00:26:49.541 --> 00:26:51.710
1000 days with tensions

00:26:54.646 --> 00:26:55.680
with my mother

00:26:55.680 --> 00:26:58.416
she said God bless you both.

00:26:58.416 --> 00:26:59.851
Thank you for joining us today.

00:26:59.851 --> 00:27:00.318
And thank you

00:27:00.318 --> 00:27:01.252
for having an opportunity

00:27:01.252 --> 00:27:02.921
to meet you earlier.

00:27:02.921 --> 00:27:04.522
You know, the incredible diversity

00:27:04.522 --> 00:27:06.091
that defines each of our nations

00:27:06.091 --> 00:27:07.926
is our strength.

00:27:08.159 --> 00:27:10.095
And the Prime Minister Trudeau and I know

00:27:10.095 --> 00:27:13.331
this is a belief that you and I share.

00:27:14.099 --> 00:27:15.567
We both build administrations

00:27:15.567 --> 00:27:16.801
that look like America

00:27:16.801 --> 00:27:19.537
and look like Canada. I'm very proud

00:27:23.308 --> 00:27:24.976
I'm very proud that

00:27:24.976 --> 00:27:25.377
both of

00:27:25.377 --> 00:27:27.812
us have cabinets that are 50% women

00:27:29.014 --> 00:27:31.549
for the first time in history.

00:27:36.287 --> 00:27:37.188
Even you don't agree,

00:27:37.188 --> 00:27:39.290
guys that stand up

00:27:47.999 --> 00:27:49.801
We took the lesson from you

00:27:49.801 --> 00:27:51.803
because the bottom line is this.

00:27:51.803 --> 00:27:52.704
We make it easier

00:27:52.704 --> 00:27:53.371
for historically

00:27:53.371 --> 00:27:54.472
underrepresented, underserved

00:27:54.472 --> 00:27:56.541
communities to dream to create, succeed.

00:27:56.841 --> 00:27:57.976
We build a better future

00:27:57.976 --> 00:27:59.611
for all our people.

00:27:59.611 --> 00:28:01.780
So let's continue the work

00:28:01.780 --> 00:28:03.782
where there are no barriers.

00:28:03.782 --> 00:28:05.383
Things look better.

00:28:05.383 --> 00:28:07.052
There are barriers to equal opportunity.

00:28:07.052 --> 00:28:08.787
We've got to tear them down.

00:28:08.787 --> 00:28:10.121
Where inequity

00:28:10.121 --> 00:28:11.222
stifles potential,

00:28:11.222 --> 00:28:12.090
where we unleash

00:28:12.090 --> 00:28:13.992
the full power of our people,

00:28:13.992 --> 00:28:15.860
where injustice holds sway

00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:17.929
Let's insist on justice being done.

00:28:19.097 --> 00:28:21.833
Those are the shared values that imbue

00:28:21.833 --> 00:28:25.103
all of our efforts are very democracy.

00:28:25.737 --> 00:28:27.906
Our vitality and our vibrancy.

00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:29.607
You know,

00:28:29.607 --> 00:28:31.476
that's what it seems that drives us all.

00:28:31.476 --> 00:28:34.112
Some places and some poor persons

00:28:34.112 --> 00:28:35.413
are kind of forgetting

00:28:35.413 --> 00:28:37.148
what the essence of democracy is.

00:28:38.450 --> 00:28:38.783
We have

00:28:38.783 --> 00:28:39.584
to reach

00:28:39.584 --> 00:28:40.085
what allows

00:28:40.085 --> 00:28:42.554
us to reach beyond the horizon.

00:28:42.554 --> 00:28:44.489
Let me close with this

00:28:45.156 --> 00:28:45.523
year.

00:28:45.523 --> 00:28:46.157
After President

00:28:46.157 --> 00:28:48.626
Kennedy spoke in Canada's parliament,

00:28:48.626 --> 00:28:49.961
he delivered a famous speech

00:28:49.961 --> 00:28:51.663
at Rice University,

00:28:51.663 --> 00:28:52.697
issuing a challenge

00:28:52.697 --> 00:28:55.033
for Americans to go to the moon.

00:28:55.033 --> 00:28:57.235
In a decade's time.

00:28:57.235 --> 00:28:59.304
You remember what he said?

00:28:59.437 --> 00:29:00.305
You probably do

00:29:00.305 --> 00:29:01.072
because we had to learn

00:29:01.072 --> 00:29:02.640
that we were in school

00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:03.241
because

00:29:03.308 --> 00:29:03.875
we choose

00:29:03.875 --> 00:29:06.878
to go to the moon in this decade

00:29:06.878 --> 00:29:07.946
and do other things,

00:29:07.946 --> 00:29:09.681
not because it's easy,

00:29:09.681 --> 00:29:12.350
but because they are hard,

00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:14.953
because that challenge is one

00:29:14.953 --> 00:29:17.122
that we are willing to accept,

00:29:17.489 --> 00:29:18.623
one that we're willing

00:29:18.623 --> 00:29:21.693
unwilling to postpone, and one

00:29:21.693 --> 00:29:23.862
which we will win.

00:29:25.029 --> 00:29:26.998
That speech tapped into something deep

00:29:26.998 --> 00:29:28.800
in America's character,

00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:31.202
something powerful, a belief

00:29:31.970 --> 00:29:33.538
that we can do big things

00:29:34.606 --> 00:29:35.406
to hold a second.

00:29:35.406 --> 00:29:36.908
Just think about it.

00:29:37.142 --> 00:29:38.176
Turn on the television

00:29:38.176 --> 00:29:39.611
the last two years,

00:29:39.611 --> 00:29:42.914
whether it's in your country or mine,

00:29:43.348 --> 00:29:45.817
after two years of covert

00:29:45.817 --> 00:29:46.818
people beginning wonder,

00:29:46.818 --> 00:29:50.822
can we still do big things, big things?

00:29:52.023 --> 00:29:55.360
We sure and how can I have

00:29:55.360 --> 00:29:57.395
that confidence

00:29:59.497 --> 00:30:01.533
I believe in every fiber of my being.

00:30:01.533 --> 00:30:03.568
That confidence can make

00:30:03.568 --> 00:30:05.270
the most audacious dreams.

00:30:05.270 --> 00:30:06.604
Reality.

00:30:06.704 --> 00:30:07.172
The lesson

00:30:07.172 --> 00:30:07.872
seven years

00:30:07.872 --> 00:30:08.673
after Kennedy's

00:30:08.673 --> 00:30:10.675
speech, the entire world watched humanity

00:30:10.875 --> 00:30:12.143
left his first footprints

00:30:12.143 --> 00:30:13.611
on those further shores.

00:30:13.611 --> 00:30:15.713
It inspired a generation

00:30:15.713 --> 00:30:16.181
that spurred

00:30:16.181 --> 00:30:17.682
much of the technology advances

00:30:17.682 --> 00:30:19.584
we now enriches our daily lives.

00:30:19.584 --> 00:30:20.852
Today,

00:30:21.019 --> 00:30:23.221
our world once more stands on the cusp

00:30:23.221 --> 00:30:24.756
of breakthroughs and possibilities

00:30:24.756 --> 00:30:25.957
that have never before

00:30:25.957 --> 00:30:27.926
even been dreamt up.

00:30:27.926 --> 00:30:29.127
In Canada

00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:30.695
and the United States are leading

00:30:30.695 --> 00:30:32.497
and will continue to lead the way

00:30:33.464 --> 00:30:36.000
in just a few days.

00:30:44.809 --> 00:30:46.911
Just a few days,

00:30:46.911 --> 00:30:47.912
Max is going to announce

00:30:47.912 --> 00:30:49.514
an international team of astronauts

00:30:49.514 --> 00:30:50.882
who will crew

00:30:51.282 --> 00:30:53.251
the Artemus two mission.

00:30:53.251 --> 00:30:54.953
The first human voyage of the moon

00:30:54.953 --> 00:30:56.955
since Apollo Mission ended

00:30:56.955 --> 00:30:59.090
more than 50 years ago

00:30:59.090 --> 00:31:01.192
will consist of three Americans

00:31:01.192 --> 00:31:02.927
and one Canadian

00:31:07.265 --> 00:31:10.134
We choose to return to the moon together.

00:31:10.969 --> 00:31:14.372
Together we return to the moon.

00:31:14.739 --> 00:31:16.507
And from there

00:31:16.507 --> 00:31:18.543
we look forward to Mars

00:31:18.543 --> 00:31:20.211
and to the limitless possibilities

00:31:20.211 --> 00:31:21.679
alive, beyond.

00:31:21.679 --> 00:31:22.480
And here on Earth,

00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:23.014
our children

00:31:23.014 --> 00:31:24.382
who watch that flight

00:31:24.382 --> 00:31:25.383
are going to learn the names

00:31:25.383 --> 00:31:27.118
of those new pioneers.

00:31:27.118 --> 00:31:27.452
They'll be

00:31:27.452 --> 00:31:29.254
the ones who carry us into the future.

00:31:29.254 --> 00:31:30.955
We hope to build

00:31:30.955 --> 00:31:32.790
the art of his generation.

00:31:32.790 --> 00:31:34.292
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:31:34.292 --> 00:31:36.361
we're living in an age of possibilities.

00:31:36.761 --> 00:31:37.428
Xi Jinping

00:31:37.428 --> 00:31:39.330
asked me in the Tibetan plateau,

00:31:39.330 --> 00:31:41.132
could I define America?

00:31:41.132 --> 00:31:42.367
And I could have said the same thing

00:31:42.367 --> 00:31:43.735
if you asked about Canada.

00:31:43.735 --> 00:31:44.469
I said yes,

00:31:44.469 --> 00:31:47.372
one word, and I made it one word.

00:31:47.805 --> 00:31:49.474
Possibilities.

00:31:49.474 --> 00:31:51.576
Nothing is beyond our capacity.

00:31:52.210 --> 00:31:53.344
We can do anything

00:31:53.344 --> 00:31:55.179
we have to never forget.

00:31:55.179 --> 00:31:56.314
We must never doubt.

00:31:56.314 --> 00:31:58.583
Our capacity can.

00:31:58.616 --> 00:31:59.584
And the United States

00:32:00.952 --> 00:32:01.352
can build

00:32:01.352 --> 00:32:04.255
big things if we stand together,

00:32:05.156 --> 00:32:08.126
hear them together, rise together.

00:32:08.126 --> 00:32:09.961
We're going to write a future together,

00:32:09.961 --> 00:32:11.429
I promise you.

00:32:11.429 --> 00:32:12.630
God bless you all.

00:32:12.630 --> 00:32:14.332
And may God protect our troops.

00:32:14.332 --> 00:32:15.199
Thank you. Thank you.

00:32:15.199 --> 00:32:16.200
Thank you.

00:32:20.571 --> 00:32:22.340
You've been watching President Biden.

00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:24.475
Biden addressed the Canadian parliament

00:32:24.475 --> 00:32:25.176
in Ottawa.

00:32:25.176 --> 00:32:27.645
The president fired up there at the end,

00:32:27.645 --> 00:32:29.881
stressing the close relationship

00:32:29.881 --> 00:32:30.782
between Canada

00:32:30.782 --> 00:32:31.816
and the United States,

00:32:31.816 --> 00:32:33.551
saying they are two countries

00:32:33.551 --> 00:32:35.853
sharing one heart.

00:32:35.853 --> 00:32:36.888
Among the biggest applause

00:32:36.888 --> 00:32:37.722
lines, the president

00:32:37.722 --> 00:32:38.990
talking about security

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:41.359
specifically in the context of Ukraine

00:32:41.693 --> 00:32:43.061
and saying these two nations

00:32:43.061 --> 00:32:43.795
are united

00:32:43.795 --> 00:32:44.929
in support of NATO's

00:32:44.929 --> 00:32:47.031
to defend against any threat.

